{"scenario":"flag","description":"fraud_model_v2 flag turned on: fraud-check latency breaks payment (+ an unrelated notify deploy)","mode":"graph","recorded_at":"2026-10-18 03:58","duration":72.64,"agent":{"duration_s":44.9,"tool_calls":10,"cost_usd":0.1368694,"input_tokens":92465,"output_tokens":2756,"report":"The frontend outage came from turning on the `fraud_model_v2` flag 17 seconds before the alert. I turned the flag back off and the frontend recovered within about 7 seconds. The page to the owning team was only recorded in the graph, so nobody has actually been notified yet.\n\n**Root cause:** change `chg-0491f0c8` set the flag from false to true (by omar, \"ramp v2 fraud model to 100%\"). fraud-check got very slow but returned no errors of its own. Its p95 went from about 15ms to about 2280ms, longer than payment's 1.5s client timeout.\n\n**Evidence path:** frontend (34\u201340% errors) \u2192 checkout (83% errors, all from its dependencies) \u2192 payment (83% errors, all from its dependencies) \u2192 fraud-check (p95 2280ms, 0% errors) \u2192 `fraud_model_v2` flag flip\n- fraud-check logs show `/work` taking 12\u201321ms, then about 2235\u20132275ms right after the flip.\n- This repeats INC-027 from 2026-09-27: same flag, same failure, fixed the same way.\n- **Ruled out:** a notify deploy (v1.2.0 \u2192 v1.2.1) 18 seconds earlier. notify stayed healthy. catalog and inventory were healthy and had no recent changes.\n\n**Action:** one action. I did a dry run of `fraud_model_v2` true \u2192 false first (it only affects fraud-check), then ran it for real (`act-878f469b`).\n\n**Verification:** `verify_recovery` on frontend showed it degraded at about 4s (15% errors), then healthy at about 7s and 10s (0% errors, p95 about 117ms).\n\n**Paging:** the message went to ananya on team risk, but no webhook is configured, so it was only saved in the graph. Someone needs to contact ananya or #team-risk directly. INC-043 is resolved and saved to incident memory.\n\n**Foll